                <pb facs="0134" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg46"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Swiss Political Department to the American Legation
                        in Switzerland </hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#flush">D. A. 58/1</p>
                <p>The Swiss Political Department has the honor to enclose herewith to the Legation
                    of the United States of America at Berne, four copies of different
                    communications which it had communicated, to the Swiss Legation at Washington to
                    be transmitted to the Government of the United States, in cables which did not
                    reach their destination.</p>
                <p>The Political Department will be extremely obliged to the Legation of the United
                    States if it would forward these different documents to their destination.</p>
                <p>The Department seizes this opportunity to renew to the Legation of the United
                    States of America, the assurances of its high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-07">December 7,
                        1918</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
